4. MCP SERVER DESIGN (PRODUCTION)
------------------------------------------------------------

ENDPOINTS:

POST /ingest
- input: raw text OR JPL packet
- output: normalized JPL graph

POST /translate/gpt
POST /translate/gemini
POST /translate/claude
- output: JPL graph

POST /diff
- input: graph_a, graph_b
- output: ΔNODE, ΔEDGE, C_cross

POST /benchmark/run
- executes corpus across models
- stores in Supabase

POST /metrics/entropy
- returns H(X), E_struct, C_eff

POST /registry/sync
- syncs YGGDRASIL index_registry with Supabase

------------------------------------------------------------
5. JARVIS GOVERNANCE RULESET (HARD LOCK)
------------------------------------------------------------

GL1: No schema mutation without version bump
GL2: No node renaming across versions
GL3: All graphs must be DAG unless explicitly marked LOOP_UNROLL
GL4: No implicit semantic inference in MCP layer
GL5: All outputs must be diff-computable
GL6: All model outputs must be traceable to source run_id
GL7: No silent registry overwrite (YGGDRASIL lock)
GL8: Supabase is source-of-record for all persistence

------------------------------------------------------------
6. YGGDRASIL INDEX REGISTRY BEHAVIOR
------------------------------------------------------------

- Every node is hashed into canonical_key
- Frequency increases stability_score
- Cross-model recurrence increases weight
- Divergence across models decreases trust_score
- Nodes with high variance become "unstable primitives"

------------------------------------------------------------
7. SHANNON LAYER (INTEGRATED METRICS)

H(X) = entropy of node distribution
H(E) = entropy of edge distribution

Compression Efficiency:
C_eff = (unique_semantic_units / total_tokens) * (1 / H(X))

Cross-model stability:
S_model = 1 - normalized variance across translations

------------------------------------------------------------
8. SYSTEM OBJECTIVE FUNCTION

Maximize:
- C_cross (model agreement)
- C_eff (compression efficiency)
- S_model (stability across models)

Minimize:
- ΔGRAPH divergence
- entropy explosion
- token redundancy

------------------------------------------------------------
9. MCP + SUPABASE AUTONOMY LOOP

LOOP:
input → MCP ingest → JPL graph →
translate models →
store outputs →
diff engine →
update registry →
reweight nodes →
retrain compression heuristics (offline)

